### Test Reminder Backend Endpoints (Professional User Context Service)
### Make sure your backend is running on https://localhost:7256

### STEP 1: Test basic endpoint first to check if service is working
GET https://localhost:7256/api/auth/current-user-context

### STEP 2: Set current user context by ID (simpler approach first)
POST https://localhost:7256/api/auth/set-user-context/2

### STEP 3: Verify current user context is set
GET https://localhost:7256/api/auth/current-user-context

### STEP 4: Test Add/Update Reminder - Backend will use current user context
POST https://localhost:7256/api/Notes/addUpdateReminderNotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "noteIdList": ["7"],
  "reminderDateTime": "2025-07-10T02:30:00.000Z"
}

### 1b. Test with PascalCase format (should also work)
POST https://localhost:7256/api/Notes/addUpdateReminderNotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "NoteIdList": ["7"],
  "ReminderDateTime": "2025-07-10T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### STEP 4: Test Remove Reminder
POST https://localhost:7256/api/Notes/removeReminderNotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "noteIdList": ["7"]
}

### STEP 5: Test with multiple notes
POST https://localhost:7256/api/Notes/addUpdateReminderNotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "noteIdList": ["7", "1"],
  "reminderDateTime": "2025-12-31T15:30:00.000Z"
}

### STEP 6: Get notes to verify reminder was added
GET https://localhost:7256/api/Notes/getNotesList

### STEP 7: Get user reminders
GET https://localhost:7256/api/Reminders

### STEP 8: Alternative - Set user context by ID
POST https://localhost:7256/api/auth/set-user-context/2

### STEP 9: Clear user context when done testing
POST https://localhost:7256/api/auth/clear-user-context
